body:
[A10] Cross-repository part of milan-fpga #629 (follow an AAF or a CRF talker's media clock, one selected source at a time; owner decision 2026-10-01). Design: milan-fpga PR #631, "Protocol-processor changes".

**RTL and microcode: none required.** The SET_CLOCK_SOURCE range check (`hdl/aecp/ucode/gen_ucode.py:1410-1440`) and the restore check (`hdl/aecp/KL_aecp_nvm_writer.sv:86-90`) already accept any index below `clock_sources_count`, over a list of any length. Line numbers are at `b2db3a97`.

## Work

- [ ] **Documentation:**
  - L6 (`docs/architecture/07_memory_maps.md:135`) and REQ-MDL-005 (`docs/00_MILAN_COMPLIANCE_REVIEW.md:420`) state Milan 5.3.3.6's set as a minimum;
  - they allow one INPUT_STREAM source per AAF input beside the CRF input's;
  - they credit BAD_ARGUMENTS to IEEE 1722.1-2021 7.2.32 and Table 7-141.
- [ ] **Tests at the top-level bench:**
  - SET_CLOCK_SOURCE over a 10-source domain accepts index 9, notifies once and reads back;
  - index 10 answers BAD_ARGUMENTS carrying the current index, and stores and notifies nothing;
  - a saved AAF index survives the D3 save and restore (REQ-AEM-013);
  - a saved index at or above a smaller image's count is refused on restore.

  Each check has a failing mutant.

## Order

This lands first, or with the parent change. The parent then bumps its submodule pin.
